  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation under RBC-TOC-02 for 5 patients. Each has a progress note.\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide raised to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum doc-00009.\n- Potassium chloride stopped (discharge summary).\n- Home omeprazole kept; the pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution and was not ordered.\n- Lisinopril: first kept on hold because post-discharge K was 5.4. A repeat BMP came in during the work (K 4.7, SCr 1.21), so I resumed lisinopril (mr-00072).\n- FLAGGED (comm-t0022):\n  - An UNSIGNED draft addendum (doc-00902) proposes furosemide 60 mg twice daily. I did not act on it.\n  - Task task-t0003 is now superseded. I couldn't cancel it, so please close it.\n- Notes: doc-t0004, doc-t0019.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg twice daily per the discharge summary.\n- A signed addendum (doc-00904) then arrived reversing it (HR 48-52, lightheaded). Carvedilol is back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016).\n- Insulin 70/30 and aspirin continued.\n- FLAGGED:\n  - Atorvastatin: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. No change made (comm-t0006).\n  - Glipizide 5 mg from Valley Endocrinology appears in the outside fill history but not in the discharge documentation. Hypoglycemia risk with insulin. Nothing ordered (comm-t0007).\n- Notes: doc-t0008, doc-t0020.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril was resumed (SCr 1.08 < 1.3, K 4.6 on 10/22).\n- A new potassium of 5.5 (10/23) then arrived, so lisinopril is back on hold (mr-00373).\n- Task task-t0018 for you, due 10/27, to review the next potassium. Please make sure the patient knows not to restart it yet.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin continued.\n- Notes: doc-t0010, doc-t0021.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr 1.12 < 1.5, K 4.4.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- The 3-day post-discharge potassium has not come in yet.\n- Note: doc-t0012.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine (1.21) is from the hospital stay, and there is no post-discharge BMP yet.\n- Task task-t0013 for you, due 10/24, to review the BMP and resume if SCr < 1.5.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- Note: doc-t0014.\n\nThe four items that arrived during the work are completed with links. Other inbox items for other patients were left untouched.",
